# Fetched artifacts for the B0 cell. The dead-man watches this directory for
# DEADMAN_CANCEL_<label>; deadman-p2.ps1 -ArtDir and babysit-b0.sh B0_CANCEL_DIR must BOTH
# point here, and the LABEL MUST BE PER-POD (a stale cancel file disarms the next dead-man at
# its first tick -- see LAUNCH-b0.md).
#
# The SMALL TEXT RECEIPTS ARE TRACKED, matching how runs/gate/*/run.json and
# runs/pod-4arm/*.DONE are tracked: B0-RESULTS.md cites them, and a citation a fresh clone
# cannot open is not a receipt. The first version of this file ignored everything, which
# would have made every receipt line in that write-up dead.
*

!.gitignore
!arm-*.json
!cell-guards.txt
!stage-timings.jsonl
!artifacts.sha256
!babysit.log
!deadman-*.log
!gpu.txt
!workspace-fs.txt
!repo-commit.txt
!bridge-health.json
!score-smoke.json
!node-version.txt
!pnpm-version.txt
!pip-pins.txt
!pod-create.json

# NOT tracked, deliberately:
#   adapter-*.tar.gz        122 MB each -- six of them
#   mc64-heldout-*.jsonl    2.4 MB each -- generation dumps, same policy as the gate's
#   pod.json / pod.id       carries the rented host's ephemeral IP; no value once terminated
#   DEADMAN_CANCEL_*        run-local state, never a receipt
